Check 1 — Does NetTracer have any data at all in your tenant (regardless of host)?
timeseries retr_pct = avg(dt.process.nettracer.retr.percent, scalar:true),
  by:{dt.entity.process_group_instance}
| fieldsAdd pgi_name = entityName(dt.entity.process_group_instance)
| fields pgi_name, retr_pct
| sort retr_pct desc
| limit 10


If this also returns nothing, NetTracer likely isn't enabled anywhere in this tenant/environment (it requires explicit activation and OneAgent version support). If it does return rows (just not for SCCM hosts), then NetTracer is on, but not yet capturing SCCM's specific processes.

Check 2 — Confirm the runs_on join isn't silently dropping everything (isolate the join from the metric)
fetch dt.entity.process_group_instance
| fieldsAdd h = runs_on[dt.entity.host]
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.host
    | filter arrayIndexOf(tags, "APMID:APP00005497") != -1
    | fields id
  ], sourceField:h, lookupField:id, prefix:"hh_"
| filter isNotNull(hh_id)
| fields id, entity.name
| limit 10
